{"claims":[{"excerpt":"The Acid Rain Program, created under Title IV","claim":"The Acid Rain Program was created under Title IV.","category":"attribution","label":"U","evidence":"EPA’s Acid Rain Program addresses sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxides from the power sector under Title IV.","narrative":"Introduce the Acid Rain Program under Title IV","narrativeRelation":"ambiguous","origin":"independently_introduced","explanation":"The source and narrative place the program under Title IV but do not establish when or how it was created.","materiality":"Low; the Title IV association is supported, but the creation claim adds an unsupported detail."},{"excerpt":"used different approaches for sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxides from the power sector","claim":"The program used different approaches for sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxides from the power sector.","category":"technical","label":"F0","evidence":"EPA’s Acid Rain Program addresses sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxides from the power sector under Title IV. The sulfur dioxide mechanism applies an aggregate cap and allows trading; one allowance covers one ton. ... The nitrogen oxides component was rate-based for certain coal-fired units, began in 1996 and did not introduce a cap or allowance trading.","narrative":"The Acid Rain Program addressed sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxides from the power sector, but it did not use one shared emissions mechanism.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source describes distinct mechanisms for the two pollutants.","materiality":"Central to the piece’s comparison."},{"excerpt":"an allowance represented permission to emit one ton under an aggregate cap","claim":"A sulfur dioxide allowance represented permission to emit one ton under an aggregate cap.","category":"technical","label":"F0","evidence":"The sulfur dioxide mechanism applies an aggregate cap and allows trading; one allowance covers one ton.","narrative":"each covered allowance represents permission for one ton under an aggregate cap with trading","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source specifies one ton per allowance under an aggregate cap; the narrative gives the same interpretation.","materiality":"Central description of the sulfur dioxide mechanism."},{"excerpt":"with allowances traded among covered sources","claim":"Allowances were traded among covered sources.","category":"technical","label":"F0","evidence":"The sulfur dioxide mechanism applies an aggregate cap and allows trading","narrative":"under an aggregate cap with trading","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"Trading is explicitly supported; the source does not separately spell out the participants, but covered sources is consistent with the program context.","materiality":"Relevant to how the sulfur dioxide mechanism operated."},{"excerpt":"Phase I began in 1995","claim":"Phase I began in 1995.","category":"chronology","label":"F0","evidence":"Its phase I began in 1995","narrative":"Phase I began in 1995","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The date matches the source.","materiality":"Relevant timeline detail."},{"excerpt":"with 263 units at 110 plants","claim":"Phase I initially included 263 units at 110 plants.","category":"quantity","label":"F0","evidence":"with 263 initial units at 110 plants","narrative":"263 initial units at 110 plants","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The unit and plant counts match; the source identifies the units as initial, which the piece does not contradict.","materiality":"Relevant coverage detail; units and plants are correctly kept distinct."},{"excerpt":"Including substitution or compensating units, the Phase I total reached 445 units.","claim":"Including substitution or compensating units, the Phase I total reached 445 units.","category":"quantity","label":"F0","evidence":"substitution or compensating units brought the phase I total to 445 units","narrati